PART A. Flat four-marker set under the full constraint list
===========================================================

join semilattices on 4 labelled elements : 76

  after K1 Resolve(Hot,Precise) = Precise    :  31 survive   (toolbox-not-policer's own worked example; accuracy is not lost to speed)
  after K2 Resolve(Cold,Hot) != Hot          :  24 survive   (I17: the storage-minimising path is not deprioritised)
  after K3 Resolve(Cold,Hot) != Cold         :   9 survive   (I5: Hot's intent is performance, and must be reachable in expressions)
  after K4 Resolve(Warm,Precise) = Precise   :   7 survive   (same argument as K1, against the default rather than against Hot)
  after K5 Resolve(Warm,Cold) != Warm        :   5 survive   (I17 again: cold storage is not silently traded for the default)
  after K6 Resolve(Warm,Hot) != Warm         :   4 survive   (I5 again: speed is not silently traded for the default)

RESULT: 4 table(s) survive all six:
  HvC=Precise HvW=Hot CvW=Cold CvP=Precise WvP=Precise HvP=Precise
  HvC=Precise HvW=Precise CvW=Cold CvP=Precise WvP=Precise HvP=Precise
  HvC=Precise HvW=Hot CvW=Precise CvP=Precise WvP=Precise HvP=Precise
  HvC=Precise HvW=Precise CvW=Precise CvP=Precise WvP=Precise HvP=Precise

Located: which minimal subsets are already unsatisfiable?

PART B. Closure under demand-union
==================================

Resolution loses nothing exactly when the strategy set is closed
under union of the demands its members carry.

  four singleton-demand markers: 4 members, 12 unresolvable pairs
      Hot v Cold needs {speed,space} and no member carries it
      Hot v Precise needs {speed,accuracy} and no member carries it
      Hot v Warm needs {speed,familiarity} and no member carries it
      Cold v Hot needs {speed,space} and no member carries it
      Cold v Precise needs {space,accuracy} and no member carries it
      Cold v Warm needs {space,familiarity} and no member carries it
      ... and 6 more
  full powerset of demands: 16 members, 0 unresolvable pairs

The powerset is closed by construction, which is the point: closure
is not something a marker set can be given, it is what a LATTICE is.
A named preset is then a point in it and naming more costs nothing
structural, which is what I1 says the design needs.

Size of the smallest closed set containing the four singletons:
  15 elements (from 4), namely:
    {speed}
    {space}
    {speed,space}
    {accuracy}
    {speed,accuracy}
    {space,accuracy}
    {speed,space,accuracy}
    {familiarity}
    {speed,familiarity}
    {space,familiarity}
    {speed,space,familiarity}
    {accuracy,familiarity}
    {speed,accuracy,familiarity}
    {space,accuracy,familiarity}
    {speed,space,accuracy,familiarity}

So closing the four presets under their own resolution generates
15 strategies. Either the design carries them, or resolution is not
a join and has to be something else.
